      "title": "READ FIRST - How to compare the two models",
      "widgets_values": [
        "TWO-MODEL LEARNED LATENT UPSCALE TEST\n\nPipeline: FastH3 Omni + VSA -> separate video/audio -> LEARNED VIDEO LATENT UPSCALE -> second H3 Ref2VA model + Turbo LoRA refinement.\n\n1. Queue as-is for text-only, or paste your prompt and connect a chosen Load Image to the conditioning reference socket. Use <Picture 1> for that reference.\n2. Pass 1: 960x544, 124 frames (~5.17 seconds), Omni NVFP4, Euler/simple, 8 steps, VSA 10%, shifts 12/3.\n3. LATENT UPSCALE: minimax_h3_latent_upscaler_3d_bf16.safetensors. Change the Scale node to adjust enlargement. Default 2x gives 1920x1088. Only video is upscaled; audio and duration stay unchanged.\n4. Pass 2: independent H3 Ref2VA model + matching Ref2V Turbo LoRA. Starts with 4 steps, denoise 0.25 and LoRA strength 1. VSA applies ONLY to Omni.\n5. Compare 01_Omni_raw (960x544) and 02_H3_refined (1920x1088) in output/FastH3_Omni_TwoModel. Both use the same generated audio.\n\nTry refinement denoise 0.15 for less change or 0.35 for stronger change; these are experimental starting points. Keep seeds fixed for comparisons. For a no-Turbo comparison, set LoRA strength to 0 and increase refinement steps. Use compatible MiniMax-H3 Ref2VA checkpoints in the second model loader. The models may swap through RAM on a 32 GB GPU. Refinement may preserve motion, identity or anatomy defects from the draft. No Builder changes are involved."
      ]
